From dc1cf11199de8f01b4c80b9bbb0fa26ba69bdeeb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 12:16:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] feat: export every role property and compare every change
 field by field

Export-RoleDefinitions.ps1
- Documented unifiedRoleDefinition properties still missing from all roles after the list call
  are fetched with one $select call and merged by id (-FetchSelect for tests).
- export-status.json next to the output folder: roles, documented, missing, properties.
  No timestamp, so it changes only with the content.
- Regression guard: a property every previous file had and no role has now stops the export
  before anything is written.

Compare-RoleSnapshots.ps1 (report schemaVersion 2.0.0)
- Permissions compared as (action, condition) pairs: addedPermissions, removedPermissions.
- Every other top-level property compared and listed in changedProperties (old, new).
- No read-only skip: every changed role is listed. readOnlyChanges is informational.
- Inheritance: roles inheriting from a changed, new or removed role are listed with
  inheritedChanges (transitive).
- schemas/entra-role-export-report-v2.json added; v1 unchanged.

Invoke-CatalogBacktest.ps1: input.json entries carry the full role definition.

entra-role-export.yml: commits export-status.json, validates against report v2.

Tests updated: the read-only test now expects the role listed and counted, and the schema tests
use v2. New tests cover export completeness and status, condition pairs, description and other
property changes, inheritance, determinism and the backtest definition field.

